WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.530
In 1991, 42.8 per cent
of the world's workers

2
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.460
had jobs in farming.

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:11.820
By 2023, that share had
fallen to 26.6 per cent.

4
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.660
Over the same years, more
and more people moved

5
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.460
to towns and cities.

6
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.010
By 2018, 55 per cent of the world's people

7
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.950
lived in urban areas.

8
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:24.350
So as countries grow richer,

9
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.330
why do workers move
from farms to factories,

10
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.120
and then to services?

11
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.870
In this mission, you'll
sort an economy into three

12
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.200
sectors and track the shift.

13
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.680
Then you'll weigh a harder question:

14
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.600
are a poor country's typical
features causes of low development,

15
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.220
or results of it?

16
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.730
Your mission: find out why
workers move from farms

17
00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:49.480
to factories and then to services
as countries grow richer.
